flowchart TD
  S([What kind of answer do you need?]) --> M[MATCH<br/>which option fits<br/>each situation?]
  S --> Q[SEQUENCE<br/>which of many activities<br/>first?]
  S --> P[SELECT<br/>pick or shortlist<br/>from a set]
  M --> MT[Decision tree<br/>red lines, then push/pull factors]
  Q --> Q1{Is it clear who does<br/>what today?}
  Q1 -- no --> RM[Responsibility mapping first]
  Q1 -- yes --> Q2
  RM --> Q2{Can do, or must do?}
  Q2 -- what we can do --> IA[Impact x availability matrix]
  Q2 -- what we must do --> EI[Eisenhower matrix]
  P --> N{How many options?}
  N -- many, about 20+ --> D{Hard data for<br/>the key tests?}
  D -- yes --> TF[Threshold filter,<br/>then assess the survivors]
  D -- no --> KO[Knock-outs, then a<br/>light scored screen]
  N -- few --> F{Must it be defensible?<br/>from tree 2}
  F -- yes --> RAG[Red/amber/green against<br/>critical success factors]
  F -- no --> Z{One design choice<br/>with 2-4 options?}
  Z -- yes --> PC[Pros and cons]
  Z -- no --> SC[Scored criteria<br/>with swing weights]
